      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.11,
          "en": "So we got our first screen output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.11,
          "end": 6.21,
          "en": "our first basic UI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.21,
          "end": 8.76,
          "en": "even though it's, of course, neither helpful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.76,
          "end": 11.07,
          "en": "nor pretty, but it's a start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.07,
          "end": 12.54,
          "en": "We achieved this by combining",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.54,
          "end": 14.55,
          "en": "the MaterialApp and Text widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.55,
          "end": 17.37,
          "en": "and passing that widget combination in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.37,
          "end": 19.17,
          "en": "to MaterialApp.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.17,
          "end": 20.7,
          "en": "Now you might notice that there are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 23.82,
          "en": "some blue squiggly lines below that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 23.82,
          "end": 27.12,
          "en": "Now, in Visual Studio code blue squiggly lines,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 30.75,
          "en": "as we have them here, mean that there isn't an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.75,
          "end": 33.3,
          "en": "but there is some improvement potential.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.3,
          "end": 35.28,
          "en": "The code is not optimal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.28,
          "end": 38.04,
          "en": "or it does something that should be changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.04,
          "end": 39.72,
          "en": "And you can hover over the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 39.72,
          "end": 41.64,
          "en": "that has these squiggly lines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 41.64,
          "end": 43.41,
          "en": "to learn more about the problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 43.41,
          "end": 46.05,
          "en": "And if you scroll down in that info box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 49.05,
          "en": "because the messages are always at the bottom,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 49.05,
          "end": 51.21,
          "en": "you see that here the recommendation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 51.21,
          "end": 53.1,
          "en": "is that we should use const",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 53.1,
          "end": 56.73,
          "en": "with the constructor to improve performance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 56.73,
          "end": 59.79,
          "en": "whatever const is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 59.79,
          "end": 62.67,
          "en": "Well, we can get rid of these blue squiggly lines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 62.67,
          "end": 66,
          "en": "by adding const in front of MaterialApp.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 66,
          "end": 68.67,
          "en": "But what is this const thing?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 68.67,
          "end": 70.41,
          "en": "Well, const is a keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 70.41,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "as you can also tell by its color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 74.76,
          "en": "It has the same color as voided import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 74.76,
          "end": 76.98,
          "en": "So it's a keyword provided by Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 76.98,
          "end": 78.81,
          "en": "built into the Dart language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 78.81,
          "end": 82.74,
          "en": "And const is a keyword and a feature that exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 82.74,
          "end": 86.61,
          "en": "to help Dart optimize the runtime performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 86.61,
          "end": 90.63,
          "en": "of your application, of your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 90.63,
          "end": 92.16,
          "en": "And how does it do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 92.16,
          "end": 94.62,
          "en": "Well, if you mark something as const,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 94.62,
          "end": 97.8,
          "en": "let's say a Text widget that you're using in your app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 97.8,
          "end": 101.34,
          "en": "then this Text widget will be stored internally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 101.34,
          "end": 104.97,
          "en": "in the memory of the device on which the app runs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 104.97,
          "end": 107.00999999999999,
          "en": "And that will always be the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 107.00999999999999,
          "end": 109.41,
          "en": "no matter if you use const or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 109.41,
          "end": 112.89,
          "en": "Once your code executes the things that are created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 112.89,
          "end": 115.41,
          "en": "by your code, the widgets, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 115.41,
          "end": 118.38,
          "en": "will be stored in the device memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 118.38,
          "end": 121.8,
          "en": "But with const, when you then use that same widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 121.8,
          "end": 124.32,
          "en": "that same widget with the same Text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 124.32,
          "end": 126.06,
          "en": "a second time in the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 126.06,
          "end": 130.98,
          "en": "that existing memory thing will be reused",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.98,
          "end": 134.73,
          "en": "instead of a second memory object being created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 134.73,
          "end": 137.91,
          "en": "So therefore, using const allows Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 137.91,
          "end": 141.69,
          "en": "to reuse values that are indeed equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 141.69,
          "end": 144.96,
          "en": "and avoids the duplication of data in memory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.96,
          "end": 147.9,
          "en": "hence making your app more memory efficient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 147.9,
          "end": 150.63,
          "en": "and improving overall performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 153.96,
          "en": "Of course, behind the scenes things are a bit more complex,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 153.96,
          "end": 156.66,
          "en": "but that is, in a nutshell, what's happening,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 156.66,
          "end": 159.39,
          "en": "and that's why you should always add const",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 159.39,
          "end": 161.07,
          "en": "when prompted for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 161.07,
          "end": 164.04,
          "en": "Now the good thing is you don't need to learn by heart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.04,
          "end": 168.57,
          "en": "in front of which widgets you should add const, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 168.57,
          "end": 171.27,
          "en": "Instead, your code editor will simply tell you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 171.27,
          "end": 173.88,
          "en": "by adding these blue squiggly lines here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 173.88,
          "end": 176.61,
          "en": "and then you should indeed add const.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 176.61,
          "end": 178.56,
          "en": "Of course, for this basic app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 178.56,
          "end": 180.21,
          "en": "it doesn't really make a difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 180.21,
          "end": 183.99,
          "en": "We're not reusing this combination of widgets anywhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 183.99,
          "end": 185.94,
          "en": "so marking it as const",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 185.94,
          "end": 188.7,
          "en": "won't give us any big advantages here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 188.7,
          "end": 190.35,
          "en": "but it also doesn't hurt,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 190.35,
          "end": 193.56,
          "en": "and it's simply a best practice to use const",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 193.56,
          "end": 196.41,
          "en": "in front of all the values where you can use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 196.41,
          "end": 200.64,
          "en": "And as you saw, using it in the right places is very simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 200.64,
          "end": 203.64,
          "en": "because your code editor simply tells you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 203.64,
          "end": 205.47,
          "en": "It, for example, also tells you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 205.47,
          "end": 209.19,
          "en": "if you're using it in a place where you should remove it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 209.19,
          "end": 212.57999999999998,
          "en": "For example, here, if I add it in front of MaterialApp",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 212.57999999999998,
          "end": 216.24,
          "en": "and in front of Text, then I get a message here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 216.24,
          "end": 219.6,
          "en": "that I'm using const unnecessarily in this place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 222.21,
          "en": "because I'm already using it in front of MaterialApp,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 222.21,
          "end": 223.86,
          "en": "which then contains Text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 223.86,
          "end": 226.62,
          "en": "so using it in front of Text in addition to that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 226.62,
          "end": 229.92000000000002,
          "en": "is simply redundant and therefore should be removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 229.92000000000002,
          "end": 232.2,
          "en": "But that's, in the end, what const does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 232.2,
          "end": 234.63,
          "en": "It allows Dart to run your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 234.63,
          "end": 236.043,
          "en": "in a more efficient way.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
